{
  "format": "pinmame-harness-scenario",
  "version": 1,
  "game": "ij_l7",
  "notes": "Boot ij_l7 from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released), navigate the service menu to T.14 IDOL TEST and start it, then press service Up six times, sampling the display and the wheel motor (public 56, custom solenoid 6) every 0.2 s. Run with --handle-mechanics 15 so PinMAME's ij_handleMech simulates all four mechanisms, including bit 3, the idol, which drives public switches 121-123 through the same three-bit sequence the known-working VPX table writes; run with --handle-mechanics 7 as the control without idol position feedback. Pass --watch-wpc-custom-switch 121/122/123 so every snapshot also reads back the idol position switches: the observations are the ROM's own test display, the motor output, and the public 121-123 levels beside each POS label.",
